-- title:
--   Approximate fixed point sequences are diametral
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. Let $(K,T)$ be normalized minimal data, so $\operatorname{diam}K=1$.
--
--   1. **Hull of the image.** $\overline{\mathrm{conv}}\,T(K)=K$, since the left side is a nonempty closed convex invariant subset.
--   2. **Diametral property (Goebel–Karlovitz).** If $\|Tu_n-u_n\|\to0$, then for every $z\in K$,
--   $$
--   \|u_n-z\|\to1 .
--   $$
--   The proof uses eventual-radius sublevel sets, which are closed, convex and invariant, together with weak compactness and minimality.
